module cognition;

import { Asked, Ruled } from cognition.signals;

// The role contract. Send a cognition an `Asked` (carrying a Query); it perceives, judges,
// and produces a `Ruled` (carrying a SETTLED Verdict). The interior is `graded`; the gate is
// the export wall (SPEC §13, §19.5) — by the consequential-action rule a consumer can only
// ever receive gated outputs, so the Jungian internals never leak.
//
// `handles A -> B` here means "consumes A events, produces B events" — a cognition runs a
// multi-step internal cascade, so it replies via an emitted `Ruled`, not a bound `<-` result
// (a single send is one provider think; see DESIGN.md §8).
pub interface Cognition { handles Asked -> Ruled; }
